// 🔴 Same investigation and same conclusion as `alter_self.ron` in this
// folder: the sheet's `variant` field is `Transform`, but the literal
// `CharacterAbility::Transform` (full stat/inventory swap, no auto-revert,
// documented admin-only — see `alter_self.ron`'s comment for the full
// citation trail) is unsuited to a reversible player spell.
//
// Unlike `alter_self`, this spell's actual mechanic — continuously scaling a
// creature's size up or down — has NO existing primitive at all, not even
// `BuffKind::Polymorphed`. `Polymorphed` swaps to a different, fully fixed
// `Body` value; it cannot scale an entity's *own* body larger or smaller.
// The dedicated size component, `comp::phys::Scale(f32)`, is never written by
// any `BuffEffect` (checked every `BuffEffect` variant in
// `common/src/comp/buff.rs` — `MovementSpeed`/`AttackDamage`/`DamageReduction`
// etc. exist, nothing touches `Scale`). Adding one would be new Rust, out of
// content-only scope.
//
// Kept branch: "enlarge" as a pure combat swing (bigger, hits harder, easier
// to hit in turn) modeled with `BuffKind::Reckless` (`common/src/comp/
// buff.rs`: "Increases both attack damage and vulnerability to damage") —
// the same primitive `magic_weapon.ron` in this folder uses for an unrelated
// "your strikes hit harder" spell, delivered here as a targeted ranged
// buff/debuff matching this batch's `earthen_grasp.ron`/`earthbind.ron`
// single-target-at-range shape (sheet range: 9m, single target) rather than
// `magic_weapon`'s self-only delivery.
// Dropped: "reduce" (the sheet's other branch — shrink, weaker attacks,
// harder to hit) has no mirror-image primitive either (no positive-evasion
// buff kind exists; `FaerieFire`'s own doc comment calls its evasion penalty
// "the mirror of `Blur`'s positive evasion", but `Blur` itself is not a real
// `BuffKind` — the comment describes a hypothetical, not shipped content).
// Also dropped: the sheet's unwilling-target branch's own save-based debuff
// framing — `Reckless` is a pure buff (no downside imposed on an unwilling
// target beyond the vulnerability side-effect built into the kind itself),
// so this ships as an ally/self-facing enlarge buff, not a hostile debuff.
// `friendly_fire: true` is required for that: `ProjectileConstructor::
// create_projectile` (`common/src/comp/projectile.rs`) targets
// `GroupTarget::OutOfGroup` by default for every `BasicRanged` attack
// (enemies only) unless `friendly_fire` is set, which switches to
// `GroupTarget::All` — the only way this school's existing single-target-at-
// range delivery shape can ever land on a chosen ally.
BasicRanged(
    energy_cost: 30,
    buildup_duration: 0.35,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    projectile: (
        kind: Simple,
        attack: Some((
            damage: 0,
            buff: Some((
                kind: Reckless,
                dur_secs: 60,
                strength: Value(0.2),
                chance: 1.0,
            )),
            friendly_fire: true,
            damage_kind: Bludgeoning,
        )),
    ),
    projectile_body: Object(BoltFire),
    projectile_speed: 55.0,
    num_projectiles: Value(1),
    meta: (
        school: Some(Transmutation),
        source: Some(Arcane),
        // level 2 spell -> min_level 12, same `level * 6` convention.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(12)),
    ),
)
